# `PluginRelation`

<SymbolMeta />

`PluginRelation` pairs one `RelationKind` with a `RelationTarget`. Plugins publish these values through `Plugin::RELATIONS`; declarations are sorted and deduplicated as part of canonical composition metadata.

<SymbolSignature />

## Semantics

`Requires` requires the target and orders it before the source. `Conflicts` prevents the source and effective target from coexisting. `Before` and `After` constrain order only when their target is present. A `RelationTarget::Plugin` selects one concrete `PluginId`; `RelationTarget::Slot` selects whichever effective implementation occupies that capability slot.

Relations describe structure before plugin code runs. They must not be used to conditionally probe runtime state or to model a contribution-level dependency. The resolver reports missing requirements, conflicts, and cycles as composition diagnostics.

See [Express composition statically](/docs/latest/extensions/plugins#express-composition-statically) for the authoring workflow and inspect `kind` and `target` when explaining a resolved plan programmatically.

<SymbolMembers />
